# H-F14 A/B for D-FREED-INODE-HOME-NEVER-PUBLISHED-LIVE-CORE-AFTER-CLEAN-UNMOUNT,
# laps 7-16 on 2/net/mesh/direct g2c (test29 test30): the continuation of
# tests/queues/recycle_sideread_ab_direct.queue on the same build
# (~/src/mxfs-e srcversion D91D7504990C6BD4175874E), the same settings and
# that queue's READING RULES unchanged, graded with the first 24 laps of the
# campaign as one.  Run from ~/src/mxfs-e.
#
# WHY MORE LAPS, AND WHY MOSTLY CONTROL (written before lap 7).  In the first
# 24 laps (recycle_sideread_ab_{caw,direct,tcp,3node}.queue) only this
# configuration reached (rs_live_reuse > 0): rsd2 and rsd4 (fix) SPASS, rsd3
# (control) SCONTROL-NO-CORRUPTION; rsd1, rsd5 and rsd6 and all 18 laps on the
# other three configurations SVACUOUS.  The rules still lack a control lap
# SCONTROL-SHOWS-CAUSE and a third fix lap with reach.  About half of this
# configuration's laps reach, and the base-rate laps show one corruption per
# two or three reaching events (lfn1 corrupt with two matches, fnt2 clean with
# one, rsd3 clean with one), so eight control laps and two fix laps.
#
# Bound: the freed_nodelay laps' 1680 s per lap (they ran 492-536 s).
1680 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots NG0_IWR_WHOLE=1 NG0_IWR_REFUSE=1 NG0_CR63_DEFER=1 NG0_IALLOC_FENCE=1 NG0_FENCE_HINT_EXEMPT=1 NG0_PEER_UNLINK=300 NG0_DRAIN_BOUND=0 NG0_PUBCLAIM_GUARD=1 NG0_SELFCLOBBER_GUARD=1 NG0_MIRROR_CHECK=1 NG0_RECYCLE_GUARD=1 NG0_FRESHSRC_GUARD=1 NG0_DELAY_MS=0 NG0_IFREE_DRAIN=1 NG0_IFREE_REAP=1 NG0_RECYCLE_SIDEREAD=0 tests/noino_gen0_ab.sh rsd7 1 300 2/net/mesh/direct g2c
